{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789802123,"nonce":"K/xKBtiKG6cyybMuramN0GctZEY=","title":"Inliner counted a box reader as a call, so the dynamic layer's small helpers never inlined","message":"`zb_box_tag` is the null check plus a call of the extern\n`zb_box_header_tag`, which the boxes pass turns into a load; `zb_any_kind`\nand `zb_any_category` are a shift and a mask over it. The inliner saw the\nextern as a call, so each was \"call-bearing\": inlined only into hot loop\nblocks, never into `zb_any_lt`, `zb_any_eq`, `zb_set_mask63` or the other\ndispatchers. Under the LLVM tier every function is compiled alone and\nreaches its callees through cells, so those three were 30 percent of\nmeteor-contest's time as separate functions.\n\nFix: a call is not a call when its callee is a box reader, by symbol or\nthrough the extern declared for it (`boxes::is_reader`). Also the set\nmask paths read a checked int box's payload directly instead of the\nchecked getter. meteor-contest 79 ms to 44 ms, nqueens 6.9 s to 5.7 s.","files":null}]}